		I should have answered your “what do you think?” directly; I missed that part of your message. I checked the current Stripe flow and SAS database.
		`event_payments` stores the customer charge amount, refunded amount, currency, Checkout Session and PaymentIntent IDs, event and organizer IDs, and payment/registration/refund statuses. There are no payout rows, and these records do not currently store the application fee, actual Stripe processing fee, or organizer transfer amount.
		Each checkout is a Stripe destination charge: SAS charges the attendee, sets an application fee, and directs the funds to the organizer’s Express account. The organizer’s effective share is ticket amount minus the application fee. Stripe deducts the card-processing cost from your platform balance, so your net is application fee minus the actual Stripe cost. That means “ticket sales minus my application fee” can calculate the organizer’s transfer, but the application fee is not the amount you ultimately keep. Stripe also groups bank payouts, so a per-event “payout to me” is more accurately “SAS net after Stripe fees.” [Stripe’s destination-charge flow](https://docs.stripe.com/connect/destination-charges.md?platform=web&ui=stripe-hosted)
